  "fullPassage": "Best Soccer Leagues in the World\n\nEnglish Premier League - England\nThe English Premier League, often called the EPL, is the highest professional soccer league in England. While it has a relatively short history, established in only 1992, it quickly rose to a position of importance. Among the 20 teams, Arsenal, Chelsea, Liverpool, Manchester City, Manchester United, and Tottenham are considered the \"Big 6.\" This league's players compete at the highest level, play at a fast pace, and have the highest level of skill of all the soccer leagues.\n\nLa Liga - Spain\nSpain's professional league, La Liga, was established in 1929 and has a total of 20 teams. Like the EPL, La Liga's teams play each other twice, for a total of 38 games each season. This league is famous for its highly technical and creative players. The world's two most famous players both played in La Liga until 2021, starring for Barcelona and Real Madrid respectively. Barcelona and Real Madrid are such strong rivals that their games are known worldwide as \"el clasico,\" meaning \"the classic.\"\n\nBundesliga - Germany\nBundesliga is Germany's highest professional soccer league. Founded in 1963, it includes a total of 18 teams from both Germany and nearby countries. Like La Liga and EPL, each team plays all the other teams twice. The league is famous for a technique called gegenpressing. This means that when a team loses control of the ball, they swiftly attack rather than retreat. While FC Bayern München is considered the strongest team, all 18 teams are known for their physical play styles and well organized strategies.",
